ther words, <MATH_0008> is a presheaf of sets on <MATH_0009>.\nNote that we have <MATH_0010>.\nWe define\n<MATH_0011>\nAs a colimit we obtain for each <MATH_0012>\na canonical map <MATH_0013>.\nFor <MATH_0014> as above there is a\ncanonical restriction map\n<MATH_0015>\ncompatible with\n<MATH_0016>\nby Categories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nIt is the unique map so that for all <MATH_0017>\nthe diagram\n<MATH_0018>\ncommutes. The uniqueness of these maps implies that we obtain a\npresheaf. This presheaf will be denoted <MATH_0019>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b4a5bb35d0b0e981414dffadcf6e6569b8516e1e502afd5c42a7f522bfe3b42f", "unit_id": "tag:00VC:prose-0002"}
